module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.SheafificationTensor
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.TensorRaisedSymmetry

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.SliceRestrictionColimits
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.TensorLocallyFree
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.TensorPreservesColimits

/-!
# Finiteness of tensor products of sheaves of modules on a ringed site

Stacks 03L6 asserts that the tensor product of two sheaves of modules on a ringed site
inherits each of the three local finiteness properties of Stacks 03DL from its two factors.
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.TensorLocallyFree` proves the locally free part;
this file proves the remaining two, that a tensor product of sheaves of finite type is of
finite type
and that a tensor product of sheaves locally generated by sections is locally generated by
sections.

Both are the same argument. A sheaf of modules is of finite type, respectively locally
generated by sections, when every object has a covering on whose members the restricted sheaf
admits a (finite) family of generating global sections. Intersecting a covering for `F` with
one for `G` gives a covering on whose members both factors have generating sections; the
tensor product of the two families generates the tensor product formed *on that member*, and
that tensor product is the restriction of the global one, so the same sections generate it.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorLocalProperties.tensorSheaf_isFiniteType`: the tensor product
  of two sheaves of modules of finite type is of finite type. This is Stacks 03L6 for the
  finite type condition Stacks 03DL(5).
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorLocalProperties.tensorSheaf_isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite`:
  the tensor product of two sheaves of modules locally generated by sections is locally
  generated by sections. This is Stacks 03L6 for Stacks 03DL(3).

## Implementation notes

The comparison `tensorOverIso` is what makes the two statements local. Both sheaves it compares are
sheafifications: the one formed on the slice is the sheafification of the tensor product of
the restricted presheaves, and the restriction of the global one receives the restriction of
the global sheafification unit, which is locally bijective on the slice topology because
`Over.forget U` is cocontinuous. The two underlying presheaves are identified by the monoidal
structure of `PresheafOfModules.pushforward₀OfCommRingCat`, exactly as in
`tensor_over_congr`, and `iso_of_locallyBijective` then transports the identification to the
two sheafifications. Comparing the two sheaves directly instead — by unfolding the restriction
of a tensor product into the tensor product of restrictions as whole structures — is what
makes this comparison expensive, and the monoidal structure avoids it.

Generating families are moved between slices by `generatingSectionsRestrict`, the image of a
family under `SheafOfModules.overMap R f`. That functor preserves colimits by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.overMap_preservesColimits` and carries the structure sheaf to the
structure sheaf by `SheafOfModules.overMapUnitIso`, which is all that
`SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.map` needs; in particular no finiteness hypothesis is
required, and since the index type is unchanged, finiteness is carried along for free.

The covering used for the finite type statement is indexed by triples consisting of a member
of each of the two given coverings together with an object admitting arrows to both. The
covering used for the locally generated statement is the iterated-slice covering supplied by
`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.CoversTop.over`, whose members come from a covering of
each member of the first covering.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03L6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03L6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GMW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GMW)
-/

public section

open CategoryTheory
open CategoryTheory.Limits
open CategoryTheory.MonoidalCategory
open CategoryTheory.BraidedCategory

universe u v w

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorLocalProperties

section Tensor

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]

/-- The tensor product of a sheaf of modules with the structure sheaf is the sheaf itself. -/
private noncomputable def tensorUnitIso (R : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w})
    (M : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w}
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf R)) :
    (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} R).obj M).obj
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf R))) ≅ M :=
  let Rsh := Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf R
  (PresheafOfModules.sheafification (𝟙 Rsh.obj)).mapIso (ρ_ M.val) ≪≫
    (asIso (PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction (𝟙 Rsh.obj)).counit).app M

/-- The tensor product of the free sheaves of modules on `I` and on `K` is the free sheaf of
modules on `I × K`. -/
private noncomputable def freeTensorIso (R : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}) (I K : Type w) :
    (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} R).obj (_root_.SheafOfModules.free
          (R := Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf R) I)).obj
              (_root_.SheafOfModules.free
          (R := Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf R) K)) ≅
      _root_.SheafOfModules.free
        (R := Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf R) (I × K) := by
  let Rsh := Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf R
  let T := (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} R).obj
    (_root_.SheafOfModules.free (R := Rsh) I)
  let _ : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{w, w} T :=
    TensorColimits.tensorLeft_preservesColimits J R _
  let _ : PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete K) T :=
    (inferInstance : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{w, w} T).preservesColimitsOfShape
  let F := _root_.SheafOfModules.freeFunctor (R := Rsh)
  have hT : IsColimit (T.mapCocone (_root_.SheafOfModules.freeCofan (R := Rsh) K)) :=
    isColimitOfPreserves T (_root_.SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan (R := Rsh) K)
  have hF : IsColimit (F.mapCocone (typeProdCocone I K)) :=
    isColimitOfPreserves F (typeProdCocone_isColimit I K)
  let η : Discrete.functor (fun _ : K => _root_.SheafOfModules.unit Rsh) ⋙ T ≅
      Discrete.functor (fun _ : K => I) ⋙ F :=
    Discrete.natIso fun _ => tensorUnitIso R (_root_.SheafOfModules.free (R := Rsh) I)
  exact hT.coconePointsIsoOfNatIso hF η ≪≫ F.mapIso (Equiv.prodComm K I).toIso

/-- The tensor product of two sheaves of modules is symmetric in its two arguments. -/
private noncomputable def tensorSwapIso {R : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}}
    (F G : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w}
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf R)) :
    ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} R).obj F).obj G ≅
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} R).obj G).obj F :=
  letI : SymmetricCategory (PresheafOfModules.{w}
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf R).obj) :=
    PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.symmetricCategory (R := R.obj)
  (PresheafOfModules.sheafification
    (𝟙 (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf R).obj)).mapIso
      (β_ F.val G.val)

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})] in
/-- The symmetry of the tensor product of sheaves of modules is natural. -/
private lemma tensorSwap_naturality {R : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}}
    {F F' G G' : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w}
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf R)}
    (f : F ⟶ F') (g : G ⟶ G') :
    (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} R).map f).app _ ≫
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} R).obj _).map g) ≫
        (tensorSwapIso F' G').hom =
      (tensorSwapIso F G).hom ≫
        (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} R).map g).app _ ≫
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} R).obj _).map f) := by
  let _ : SymmetricCategory (PresheafOfModules.{w}
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf R).obj) :=
    PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.symmetricCategory (R := R.obj)
  let sh := PresheafOfModules.sheafification
    (𝟙 (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf R).obj)
  refine (congrArg (fun morphism ↦ morphism ≫ (tensorSwapIso F' G').hom)
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor_uncurry_map R f g)).trans ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (congrArg (fun morphism ↦ (tensorSwapIso F G).hom ≫ morphism)
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor_uncurry_map R g f).symm)
  change sh.map (f.val ⊗ₘ g.val) ≫ sh.map (β_ F'.val G'.val).hom =
    sh.map (β_ F.val G.val).hom ≫ sh.map (g.val ⊗ₘ f.val)
  rw [← Functor.map_comp, ← Functor.map_comp]
  exact congrArg sh.map (braiding_naturality f.val g.val)

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})] in
private lemma tensorMap_epi (ring : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w})
    {left leftTarget right rightTarget : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w}
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf ring)}
    (leftHom : left ⟶ leftTarget) (rightHom : right ⟶ rightTarget) [Epi leftHom] [Epi rightHom] :
    Epi (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} ring).map leftHom).app right ≫
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} ring).obj leftTarget).map rightHom)
          := by
  have preserves_epi : ∀ (T : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w}
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf ring) ⥤
      _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf ring))
      [PreservesColimitsOfSize.{w, w} T] {a b : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w}
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf ring)} (h : a ⟶ b) [Epi h], Epi (T.map h) := by
    intro T _ a b h _
    have : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{0, 0} T := preservesColimitsOfSize_shrink _
    exact preserves_epi_of_preservesColimit T h
  have _ : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{w, w}
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} ring).flip.obj right) :=
    TensorRaised.tensorRightRaised_preservesColimits.{u, v, w, w} ring right
  have _ : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{w, w}
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} ring).obj leftTarget) :=
    TensorColimits.tensorLeft_preservesColimits J ring leftTarget
  exact @epi_comp _ _ _ _ _ _
    (preserves_epi ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} ring).flip.obj right)
      leftHom) _
    (preserves_epi ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} ring).obj leftTarget)
      rightHom)

/-- Generating sections of two sheaves of modules give generating sections of their tensor
product, indexed by the product of the two index types. -/
private noncomputable def tensorGeneratingSections {R : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}}
    (F G : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf R))
    (s : F.GeneratingSections) (t : G.GeneratingSections) :
    (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} R).obj F).obj G).GeneratingSections
        := by
  let rightFree := _root_.SheafOfModules.free
    (R := Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf R) t.I
  let tensorMap :=
    ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} R).map s.π).app rightFree ≫
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} R).obj F).map t.π
  have tensorMapEpi : Epi tensorMap := tensorMap_epi R s.π t.π
  refine ⟨s.I × t.I,
    (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, v, w, w, w} R).obj F).obj G).freeHomEquiv
      ((freeTensorIso R s.I t.I).inv ≫ tensorMap), ?_⟩
  rw [Equiv.symm_apply_apply]
  exact @epi_comp _ _ _ _ _ _ (by infer_instance) _ tensorMapEpi

end Tensor

section Restrict

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [∀ U : C, HasWeakSheafify (J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [∀ U : C, (J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- A family of generating sections of a sheaf of modules on the slice over `U` restricts
along an arrow `f : V ⟶ U` to a family of generating sections on the slice over `V`. The
index type is unchanged. -/
private noncomputable def generatingSectionsRestrict {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}}
    {M : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} R} {V U : C} (f : V ⟶ U)
    (s : (M.over U).GeneratingSections) : (M.over V).GeneratingSections :=
  letI : HasSheafify (J.over V) AddCommGrpCat.{w} :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.hasSheafify_of_locallyBijective
  letI : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{w, w} (_root_.SheafOfModules.overMap R f) :=
    overMap_preservesColimits R f
  _root_.SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.equivOfIso
    ((_root_.SheafOfModules.overFunctorMap R f).app M)
    (s.map (_root_.SheafOfModules.overMap R f)
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.overMapUnitIso f).symm)

private lemma generatingSectionsRestrict_index {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}}
    {M : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} R} {V U : C} (f : V ⟶ U)
    (s : (M.over U).GeneratingSections) : (generatingSectionsRestrict f s).I = s.I := rfl

end Restrict

section Slice

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]

/-- A slice of a site on which commutativity can be forgotten from sheaves of rings inherits
that property, since forgetting it preserves limits of every size. -/
instance hasSheafCompose_over (U : C) :
    (J.over U).HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w}) :=
  letI : PreservesLimitsOfSize.{v, max u v} (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w}) :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.preservesLimitsOfSize_forget₂_commRingCat_ringCat
  hasSheafCompose_of_preservesLimitsOfSize (J.over U)

variable [∀ U : C, HasWeakSheafify (J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [∀ U : C, (J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- The tensor product of two sheaves of modules formed on the slice site over `U` is the
restriction to that slice of the tensor product formed on the whole site. -/
noncomputable def tensorOverIso (O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}) (U : C)
    (F G : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w}
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)) :
    ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor (O.over U)).obj (F.over U)).obj (G.over U) ≅
      (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor O).obj F).obj G).over U := by
  let R := Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O
  let L := presheafRestriction R.obj U
  let pf := PresheafOfModules.pushforward₀OfCommRingCat.{w} (Over.forget U) O.obj
  letI : MonoidalCategory (PresheafOfModules.{w} (R.over U).obj) :=
    PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.monoidalCategory (R := (Over.forget U).op ⋙ O.obj)
  let f := sheafificationUnit (R := R.over U) ((F.over U).val ⊗ (G.over U).val)
  let g := L.map (sheafificationUnit (R := R) (F.val ⊗ G.val))
  let e : (F.over U).val ⊗ (G.over U).val ≅ L.obj (F.val ⊗ G.val) :=
    Functor.Monoidal.μIso pf F.val G.val
  have hfi : PresheafOfModules.IsLocallyInjective (J.over U) f :=
    inferInstanceAs (Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective (J.over U)
      (CategoryTheory.toSheafify (J.over U) ((F.over U).val ⊗ (G.over U).val).presheaf))
  have hfs : PresheafOfModules.IsLocallySurjective (J.over U) f :=
    inferInstanceAs (Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (J.over U)
      (CategoryTheory.toSheafify (J.over U) ((F.over U).val ⊗ (G.over U).val).presheaf))
  have hgi : PresheafOfModules.IsLocallyInjective (J.over U) g :=
    Presheaf.isLocallyInjective_whisker (J.over U) J (Over.forget U)
      (CategoryTheory.toSheafify J (F.val ⊗ G.val).presheaf)
  have hgs : PresheafOfModules.IsLocallySurjective (J.over U) g :=
    Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_whisker (J.over U) J (Over.forget U)
      (CategoryTheory.toSheafify J (F.val ⊗ G.val).presheaf)
  exact iso_of_locallyBijective (hfi := hfi) (hfs := hfs) (hgi := hgi) (hgs := hgs)
    (R := R.over U) f g e

/-- Generating sections of the two factors over a member of a covering give generating
sections of the tensor product over that member, with index type the product of the two. -/
private noncomputable def tensorOverGeneratingSections (O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}) (U : C)
    (F G : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w}
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O))
    (s : (F.over U).GeneratingSections) (t : (G.over U).GeneratingSections) :
    ((((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor O).obj F).obj G).over U).GeneratingSections :=
  _root_.SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.equivOfIso (tensorOverIso O U F G)
    (tensorGeneratingSections (R := O.over U) (F.over U) (G.over U) s t)

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})] in
private lemma tensorOverGeneratingSections_index (O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}) (U : C)
    (F G : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w}
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O))
    (s : (F.over U).GeneratingSections) (t : (G.over U).GeneratingSections) :
    (tensorOverGeneratingSections O U F G s t).I = (s.I × t.I) := rfl

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 03L6, finite type case.** The tensor product of two sheaves of
modules of finite type on a ringed site is of finite type. -/
@[stacks 03L6 "finite_type", instance]
theorem tensorSheaf_isFiniteType (X : AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.{u, v, w})
    [X.J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
    [HasWeakSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    [∀ U : X.C, HasWeakSheafify (X.J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    [∀ U : X.C, (X.J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    (F G : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
    [_root_.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType F] [_root_.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType G] :
    _root_.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType
      (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor X.O).obj F).obj G) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨qF, hqF⟩ := _root_.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.exists_localGeneratorsData F
  obtain ⟨qG, hqG⟩ := _root_.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.exists_localGeneratorsData G
  let I := Σ i : qF.I, Σ j : qG.I,
    {V : X.C // Nonempty ((V ⟶ qF.X i) × (V ⟶ qG.X j))}
  let Y (z : I) := z.2.2.1
  let gens (z : I) :=
    tensorOverGeneratingSections X.O (Y z) F G
      (generatingSectionsRestrict (Classical.choice z.2.2.2).1 (qF.generators z.1))
      (generatingSectionsRestrict (Classical.choice z.2.2.2).2 (qG.generators z.2.1))
  refine ⟨{ I := I, X := Y, generators := gens, coversTop := ?_ }, ⟨fun z => ?_⟩⟩
  · intro W
    exact X.J.transitive (qF.coversTop W) (Sieve.ofObjects Y W) (by
      intro V f hf
      refine X.J.superset_covering ?_ (qG.coversTop V)
      intro Z g hg
      obtain ⟨i, ⟨b⟩⟩ := (Sieve.mem_ofObjects_iff qF.X f).mp hf
      obtain ⟨j, ⟨c⟩⟩ := (Sieve.mem_ofObjects_iff qG.X g).mp hg
      exact (Sieve.mem_ofObjects_iff Y (g ≫ f)).2 ⟨⟨i, j, Z, ⟨(g ≫ b, c)⟩⟩, ⟨𝟙 Z⟩⟩)
  · have _ : (qF.generators z.1).IsFiniteType := hqF.isFiniteType z.1
    have _ : (qG.generators z.2.1).IsFiniteType := hqG.isFiniteType z.2.1
    refine ⟨?_⟩
    change Finite ((qF.generators z.1).I × (qG.generators z.2.1).I)
    infer_instance

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 03L6, locally generated case.** The tensor product of two sheaves of
modules locally generated by sections on a ringed site is locally generated by sections. -/
@[stacks 03L6 "locally_generated"]
theorem tensorSheaf_isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite
    (X : AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.{u, v, w})
    [X.J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
    [HasWeakSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    [∀ U : X.C, HasWeakSheafify (X.J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    [∀ U : X.C, (X.J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    (F G : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
    (hF : _root_.SheafOfModules.IsLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite F)
    (hG : _root_.SheafOfModules.IsLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite G) :
    _root_.SheafOfModules.IsLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite
      (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor X.O).obj F).obj G) := by
  intro U
  obtain ⟨I, V, hV, hFV⟩ := hF U
  choose K W hW hGW using fun i : I => hG (V i).left
  have hB (i : I) : ((X.J.over U).over (V i)).CoversTop
      fun j => (V i).iteratedSliceBackward.obj (W i j) := by
    intro Z
    refine ((X.J.over U).over (V i)).pullback_stable
      ((V i).iteratedSliceEquiv.unitIso.app Z).hom
      (((X.J.over U).over (V i)).superset_covering
        (Sieve.functorPushforward_ofObjects_le (V i).iteratedSliceBackward (W i)
          ((V i).iteratedSliceEquiv.functor.obj Z)) ?_)
    exact (Functor.IsDenseSubsite.coverPreserving (J := X.J.over (V i).left)
      (K := (X.J.over U).over (V i)) (V i).iteratedSliceEquiv.inverse).cover_preserve
        (hW i ((V i).iteratedSliceEquiv.functor.obj Z))
  refine ⟨(i : I) × K i,
    fun ij => ((V ij.1).iteratedSliceBackward.obj (W ij.1 ij.2)).left,
    hV.over hB, fun ij => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨s⟩ := hFV ij.1
  obtain ⟨t⟩ := hGW ij.1 ij.2
  exact ⟨tensorOverGeneratingSections X.O (W ij.1 ij.2).left F G
    (generatingSectionsRestrict (W ij.1 ij.2).hom s) t⟩

end Slice

end Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorLocalProperties

